---
// Our Story: 1637 heritage, free house, and revival narrative.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import SectionHeader from './SectionHeader.astro';
import storyImg from '../assets/photos/story-fireplace.jpg';
---

<section id="story" class="bg-white px-5 py-20 sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl">
    <SectionHeader eyebrow="Est. 1637" title="Our Story">
      {/* ship icon */}
      <svg class="h-6 w-6" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M3 15l1.6 3.2a2 2 0 0 0 1.8 1.1h11.2a2 2 0 0 0 1.8-1.1L21 15M5 15h14l-2-4H7l-2 4zM12 3v8M12 3l3 2M12 3L9 5" />
      </svg>
    </SectionHeader>

    <div class="mt-12 grid items-center gap-10 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:gap-14">
      <Image
        src={storyImg}
        alt="The Old Ship's cosy interior with a lit wood-burning stove set in an exposed-brick inglenook, copper pans and brass plaques"
        widths={[480, 768, 1100]}
        sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 50vw, 100vw"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover shadow-lg shadow-navy/10 ring-1 ring-navy/10"
      />

      <div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink/80">
        <p>
          Tucked just off the Marlow Road in the village of Cadmore End, The Old Ship is the sort of
          pub England does best: low beams, a warm welcome and no airs about it. There's been an inn
          on this spot <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">since 1637</strong>, which means beer has
          been poured here for the best part of four centuries.
        </p>
        <p>
          For generations it was the heart of the village, and after a long spell with its doors
          closed, it's open once more, back to doing what it always did well: honest food, well-kept
          ale and good company.
        </p>
        <p>
          As a <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">free house</strong>, we answer to no brewery. The
          beers on our pumps are there because they're good, not because we're told to pour them. Most
          come from breweries right on our doorstep.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
